red clearing the  way for the netflix version  in 2011 marvel television showed up at  san diego comic-con with a whole slew of  high-profile tv projects to show off  these included early versions of jessica  jones and cloak and dagger as well as  one show that never got made mockingbird  yes the future agents of shield  character was once set to headline her  own tv show for abc family it would have  been very different though marvel  television head jeff loeb revealed it  was about a young bobby morse who as a  freshman science whiz at a silicon  valley university gets recruited by  shield and has to balance spywork with  the life of a normal student this  proposed mockingbird show seemed like a  natural fit for abc family's programming  lineup however no further news emerged  after all the razzle dazzle of an sdcc  announcement of course a new incarnation  of morse went on to be a pivotal part of  agents of shield closing the book on  this mockingbird tv show speaking of  which  following the demise of her planned abc  family show mockingbird got a second  shot at headlining a television program  with marvel's most wanted a proposed  agents of shield spin-off this would  have seen bobby morse and lance hunter  going on the lamb to have their own  action-filled adventures separate from  phil coulson and company that's the fun  stuff i love doing the action the show  had numerous stops and starts with abc  passing on the show in may of 2015 only  for the network to revive their interest  by the end of the summer  the pilot was shot in early 2016 and  agents of shield even built up the  spin-off by giving morse and hunter a  concrete farewell despite all this  marvel's most wanted met a discouraging  demise abc passed on the pilot in may of  2016 saying that it was quote not as  strong as some of the other pilots that  we shot  in the mid 2010s 20th century fox got  busy expanding the x-men over to tv with  legion airing on fx and the gifted  playing on fox one other proposed fox  program was hellfire which would have  centered on the villainous hellfire club  at the likes of sebastian shaw and emma  frost belong to the group previously  appeared in x-men first class and the  show would have followed the adventures  of an agent who infiltrates the evil  organization but hellfire never got off  the ground beyond an initial  announcement and a vague promise to air  in 2016.  after the show was confirmed to be dead  producer lauren schuller donner revealed  the reason behind dumping hellfire  simply stating quote it was too many  characters and not enough depth of  character  the bigger they are  the more pieces they make  following the success of shows like rick  and morty it looked like marvel  television was aiming to make a big  swing in the adult cartoon genre through  a series of cartoons on hulu among those  proposed shows was a series titled tigra  and dazzler which would have starred the  two titular superheroes as imagined  through the comedic filter of chelsea  handler  sadly trouble emerged for the project in  december of 2019 when it was first  reported that the show's writing staff  had been fired though handler remained  tigra and dazzler was eventually  canceled the following month the demise  came about as marvel studios took over  control of marvel television with the  division deciding to shift its focus  over to programming for the disney plus  streaming service  though he started out as a minor player  in the comics brother voodoo has become  quite a prominent character in his own  right in fact he's garnered such  importance that he even took the  sorcerer supreme mantle from dr strange  no wonder then that such a notable  superhero would be eyeballed for a tv  series with the sci-fi network looking  to get a brother voodoo show off the  ground way back in 2003 the plan for  voodoo was to film a 2-hour tv movie  that could also double as a pilot for a  proposed series but it never got beyond  the press release still though his  sci-fi series went nowhere there's hope  yet for another brother voodoo  adaptation the appearance of his twin  brother daniel drumm and doctor strange  indicates he could have a future in the  marvel cinematic universe  poor howard the duck his solo  adaptations into other media rarely go  well despite being an incredibly popular  comic book character in the 1970s  howard's reputation was tainted by a  legendarily bad 1986 movie  you think i might find happiness in the  animal kingdom ducky  like they say thou love's strange  we could always give it a try and his  misfortune didn't end there after  decades of being a supporting figure in  the comics howard was poised to return  to leading duck status thanks to a  proposed hulu cartoon that never saw the  light of day the show was announced  alongside a slew of other hulu marvel  cartoons aimed at adult audiences each  of them were handed high-profile  behind-the-scenes talent with kevin  smith placed in charge of howard the  duck smith said let's be honest i'm not  talented enough to handle any of the  avengers but howard is definitely in my  wheelhouse his enthusiasm was palpable  but unfortunately it wasn't enough to  ensure the show made it onto hulu howard  the duck was cancelled roughly a year  after it was first announced with marvel  studios putting its focus on disney plus  series instead smith reacted to the news  with an appropriate statement on twitter  saying alas howard remains trapped in a  world he never made  that's it  no more mr nice duck  on the big screen marvel teamed up  superheroes for the avengers on netflix  its street level heroes created the  defenders for their planned hulu  cartoons marvel opted to go in a  different more comical direction by  merging warped irrelevant characters to  create the offenders a team-up between  howard the duck tigra and dazzler modoc  and hit monkey the show would have been  the culmination of all of hulu and  marvel's forays into adult 