nced  ridley would be writing some comics for  them but so far nothing on screen has  materialized  at one point in time marvel and abc were  keen on producing half-hour comedies  like damage control focusing on a  company that cleans up after superhero  battles damage control had a premise  that seemed ripe for both television and  for generating humorous situations abc  president paul lee noted in january 2016  that damage control is the one that's  going to be coming out this season we  hope it's going to be great in the end  though damage control was just one of  the many proposed tv shows that died on  the vine instead the group found its way  into the mcu through spider-man  homecoming at least keeping alive the  possibility we may see them again in  some form or another  at one point in time a new warriors show  starring squirrel girl as the leader of  a group of teenage superheroes was set  to be a major deal for the freeform  network not only would it have been a  major superhero series but it was set to  launch a bunch of spin-offs freeform's  carrie burke said the characters they've  chosen are all really singular and could  each carry the show that they're on  they're bound together as a band of  underdogs for as long as we choose with  this show but it's conceptually  tailor-made for spin-offs none of those  plans would ever see the light of day  though as new warriors was abruptly  dropped by freeform and even though new  warriors had a set cast and a finished  pilot producers failed to attract the  show a new home despite marvel  television's best efforts to find a new  network new warriors was ultimately  canned in 2019  after atlanta became a breakout success  fx wanted to continue being in the  donald glover business meanwhile the  colossal box office success of deadpool  meant that the entire fox conglomerate  wanted to put the hero in everything  these two desires collided with a  proposed cartoon for grown-ups that  would air on fxx and be spearheaded by  glover despite the show being littered  with talent though news broke in march  of 2018 that it wasn't going forward  glover took to twitter to deliver a  scathing 15-page script in which  deadpool explains why the show was never  made attributing the show's demise to  marketing concerns from marvel fx head  john landgraf later clarified that  marvel had pulled the plug and that fx  was still behind the program despite  deadpool co-creator rob lyfield saying  in may of 2019 that a new version of  this project was on the way no further  news on a raunchy deadpool tv cartoon  has emerged this merc with a mouth may  be unkillable as a character but his tv  show has ended up as dead as a doornail  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite marvel shows are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Applause]  [Music]  you

